{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-124114" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The affine transformation $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nx=u+v,\\,y=u+2v+1.\n$$\n\nGiven that the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ of $T$ is\n\n$$\nu=ax-y+1,\\,v=by-x+c,\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b+c?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066229/state.json" "file_sha256" "9116a698da59476176d885632a2a312ea08e061282fca84da9e0cceb4fd30b38"} {"question" "q-124114" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nReversing the action of $T,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Au+b & =x \\\\ Au & =x-b \\\\ u & ={A}^{-1}(x-b).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, writing our transformation in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}u+v \\\\ u+2v+1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u+v \\\\ u+2v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the inverse of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 1}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u} & ={{[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{A}^{-1}}\\cdot ({{[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}-{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot x+(-1)\\cdot (y-1) \\\\ (-1)\\cdot x+1\\cdot (y-1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2x-y+1 \\\\ y-x-1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ in coordinate form is\n\n$$\nu=2x-y+1,\\,v=1y-x+(-1).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=2+1+(-1)=2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066229/state.json" "file_sha256" "9116a698da59476176d885632a2a312ea08e061282fca84da9e0cceb4fd30b38"} {"question" "q-124114" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066229/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9e4a3feec82f927cadd394f9db04f8cb10a33bd18f4477e0f34e4475c0897adb"} {"question" "q-124114" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066229/state.json" "file_sha256" "9116a698da59476176d885632a2a312ea08e061282fca84da9e0cceb4fd30b38"} {"question" "q-124114" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066229/state.json" "file_sha256" "9116a698da59476176d885632a2a312ea08e061282fca84da9e0cceb4fd30b38"} {"question" "q-124114" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066229/state.json" "file_sha256" "9116a698da59476176d885632a2a312ea08e061282fca84da9e0cceb4fd30b38"} {"question" "q-124117" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The matrix form of the affine transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind $a+b+c,$ given that the matrix form of the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ c\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066229/state.json" "file_sha256" "9116a698da59476176d885632a2a312ea08e061282fca84da9e0cceb4fd30b38"} {"question" "q-124117" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nReversing the action of $T,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Au+b & =x \\\\ Au & =x-b \\\\ u & ={A}^{-1}(x-b).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe matrix form of $T$ gives us the following information:\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the inverse of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 5}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-1}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u} & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{A}^{-1}}\\cdot ({{[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}-{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=-2+1+(-8)=-9.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066229/state.json" "file_sha256" "9116a698da59476176d885632a2a312ea08e061282fca84da9e0cceb4fd30b38"} {"question" "q-124117" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066229/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9e4a3feec82f927cadd394f9db04f8cb10a33bd18f4477e0f34e4475c0897adb"} {"question" "q-124117" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066229/state.json" "file_sha256" "9116a698da59476176d885632a2a312ea08e061282fca84da9e0cceb4fd30b38"} {"question" "q-124117" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-11"] ["math" "-8"] ["math" "-9"] ["math" "11"] ["math" "7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066229/state.json" "file_sha256" "9116a698da59476176d885632a2a312ea08e061282fca84da9e0cceb4fd30b38"} {"question" "q-124117" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-9"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066229/state.json" "file_sha256" "9116a698da59476176d885632a2a312ea08e061282fca84da9e0cceb4fd30b38"} {"question" "q-124235" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The matrix form of the affine transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind $a+b+c,$ given that the matrix form of the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ a & b\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ c\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066229/state.json" "file_sha256" "9116a698da59476176d885632a2a312ea08e061282fca84da9e0cceb4fd30b38"} {"question" "q-124235" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nReversing the action of $T,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Au+b & =x \\\\ Au & =x-b \\\\ u & ={A}^{-1}(x-b).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe matrix form of $T$ gives us the following information:\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the inverse of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{-2\\cdot (-3)-2\\cdot 4}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u} & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{A}^{-1}}\\cdot ({{[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}-{{[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ \\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=2+\\frac{3}{2}+(-\\frac{5}{2})=1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066229/state.json" "file_sha256" "9116a698da59476176d885632a2a312ea08e061282fca84da9e0cceb4fd30b38"} {"question" "q-124235" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066229/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9e4a3feec82f927cadd394f9db04f8cb10a33bd18f4477e0f34e4475c0897adb"} {"question" "q-124235" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066229/state.json" "file_sha256" "9116a698da59476176d885632a2a312ea08e061282fca84da9e0cceb4fd30b38"} {"question" "q-124235" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066229/state.json" "file_sha256" "9116a698da59476176d885632a2a312ea08e061282fca84da9e0cceb4fd30b38"} {"question" "q-124235" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066229/state.json" "file_sha256" "9116a698da59476176d885632a2a312ea08e061282fca84da9e0cceb4fd30b38"} {"question" "q-124315" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The affine transformation $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nx=5u-9v-2,\\,y=4u-8v+4.\n$$\n\nGiven that the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ of $T$ is\n\n$$\nu=ax-\\frac{9}{4}y+b,\\,v=cx-\\frac{5}{4}y+7.\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b+c?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066229/state.json" "file_sha256" "9116a698da59476176d885632a2a312ea08e061282fca84da9e0cceb4fd30b38"} {"question" "q-124315" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nReversing the action of $T,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Au+b & =x \\\\ Au & =x-b \\\\ u & ={A}^{-1}(x-b).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, writing our transformation in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5u-9v-2 \\\\ 4u-8v+4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5u-9v \\\\ 4u-8v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}5 & -9 \\\\ 4 & -8\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the inverse of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{-8\\cdot 5-(-9)\\cdot 4}[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 9 \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-4}[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 9 \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -\\frac{9}{4} \\\\ 1 & -\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u} & ={{[\\begin{aligned}2 & -\\frac{9}{4} \\\\ 1 & -\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{A}^{-1}}\\cdot ({{[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}-{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -\\frac{9}{4} \\\\ 1 & -\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x+2 \\\\ y-4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot (x+2)-\\frac{9}{4}\\cdot (y-4) \\\\ 1\\cdot (x+2)+(-\\frac{5}{4})\\cdot (y-4)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2x-\\frac{9}{4}y+13 \\\\ x-\\frac{5}{4}y+7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ in coordinate form is\n\n$$\nu=2x-\\frac{9}{4}y+13,\\,v=1x-\\frac{5}{4}y+7.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=2+13+1=16.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066229/state.json" "file_sha256" "9116a698da59476176d885632a2a312ea08e061282fca84da9e0cceb4fd30b38"} {"question" "q-124315" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066229/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9e4a3feec82f927cadd394f9db04f8cb10a33bd18f4477e0f34e4475c0897adb"} {"question" "q-124315" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066229/state.json" "file_sha256" "9116a698da59476176d885632a2a312ea08e061282fca84da9e0cceb4fd30b38"} {"question" "q-124315" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "16"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "7"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066229/state.json" "file_sha256" "9116a698da59476176d885632a2a312ea08e061282fca84da9e0cceb4fd30b38"} {"question" "q-124315" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "16"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066229/state.json" "file_sha256" "9116a698da59476176d885632a2a312ea08e061282fca84da9e0cceb4fd30b38"} {"question" "q-162196" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066229/assets/576d60f179b56159504efc59178ada3db798046d01a7dbc92986cd1162f770ea.png)\n\nConsider the affine transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nx=u+2v+1,\\,y=2u+v-1.\n$$\n\nWhat would be the image of the square shown above under the action of $T?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066229/state.json" "file_sha256" "9116a698da59476176d885632a2a312ea08e061282fca84da9e0cceb4fd30b38"} {"question" "q-162196" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that for any affine transformation \n\n$$\nT:u⟶Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix and $u$ and $b$ are $2\\times 1$ column vectors, we have one of the following three possibilities:\n\n- If $T$ is non-singular, i.e., when $det(A)\\ne 0,$ then the image of a two-dimensional object is a two-dimensional object. In particular, the image of a polygon with $n$ vertices is a polygon with $n$ vertices.\n\n- If $T$ is singular, i.e., when $det(A)=0,$ we have two additional subcases:\n\n- If $A$ has at least one nonzero entry, then the image of a two-dimensional object is a one-dimensional line segment.\n\n- If $A$ is the zero matrix, then the image of a two-dimensional object is a point on the plane.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our transformation.\n\nThe given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}u+2v+1 \\\\ 2u+v-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u+2v \\\\ 2u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nComputing the determinant of $A,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot 1-2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-3 \\\\  & \\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a non-singular matrix. \n\nTherefore, $T$ is invertible and the image of the square under the action of $T$ is a parallelogram." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066229/state.json" "file_sha256" "9116a698da59476176d885632a2a312ea08e061282fca84da9e0cceb4fd30b38"} {"question" "q-162196" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066229/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9e4a3feec82f927cadd394f9db04f8cb10a33bd18f4477e0f34e4475c0897adb"} {"question" "q-162196" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066229/state.json" "file_sha256" "9116a698da59476176d885632a2a312ea08e061282fca84da9e0cceb4fd30b38"} {"question" "q-162196" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "A cube"] ["text" "A line segment"] ["text" "A parallelogram"] ["text" "A point"] ["text" "A triangle"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066229/state.json" "file_sha256" "9116a698da59476176d885632a2a312ea08e061282fca84da9e0cceb4fd30b38"} {"question" "q-162196" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "A parallelogram"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066229/state.json" "file_sha256" "9116a698da59476176d885632a2a312ea08e061282fca84da9e0cceb4fd30b38"}] "usage" {"q-124114" [] "q-124117" []} "basis" 2227 "retractions" [[17592186179925 :question/problem "The affine transformation $T$ is defined as\n\n$x = u + v, y = u + 2v + 1$.\n\nGiven that the inverse transformation $T^{-1}$ of $T$ is\n$u = ax - y + 1, v = by - x + c$,\nwhat is the value of $a + b + c$?"] [17592186179926 :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nFind $a + b + c$, given that the matrix form of the inverse transformation $T^{-1}$ is given by\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}a & b \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ c\\end{bmatrix}$."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186177551 17592186177552 17592186177553 17592186177554 17592186177555 17592186177557 17592186177558 17592186177559 17592186177560 17592186177561] "immutable_fields" [[17592186177550 :answer-field/correct] [17592186177550 :answer-field/id] [17592186177550 :answer-field/key] [17592186177550 :answer-field/type] [17592186177556 :answer-field/correct] [17592186177556 :answer-field/id] [17592186177556 :answer-field/key] [17592186177556 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
